    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10451" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consectĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		conseco, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a cutting</i> or <i>cleaving to
			pieces</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arborum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 60, 151</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nisi consectionis ejus (materiae) fabricam
					haberemus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the art of fashioning it</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Div. 1, 51, 116</span></i>
			.</div>
